TestMind is a commercial product. This repository is public so that schools,
parents, students and researchers can inspect how the test works and what it
does with a student's answers — transparency about an instrument given to
minors is the point. Public visibility is not an open-source licence.

No permission is granted to copy, modify, redistribute, republish or create
derivative works from any part of this repository, including but not limited to:

  - the test application and scoring logic (test.html, assets/*.js)
  - the item banks and their translations (tools/*_content*.py)
  - the career, major, subject and work-value taxonomy (tools/careers.py)
  - the character artwork and the ten archetype guides (assets/characters/,
    assets/characters.js, guides/)
  - the site text in Uzbek, Russian and English

You may read this code, link to the live site, and quote short excerpts with
attribution for review, teaching or journalism.

The test draws on publicly available frameworks — the Big Five trait model and
the RIASEC interest model, including the U.S. Department of Labor's O*NET
Interest Profiler, which is in the public domain. Those underlying frameworks
are not claimed here. The items, wording, translations, taxonomy, artwork and
scoring in this repository are original work and are claimed.

Fonts under assets/fonts/ are third-party and not covered by this notice. Inter
and Bitter are both licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, which permits
their redistribution here and governs any reuse of those two files.

